Description: Put touched PWM channels into a safe state on shutdown and reboot
 The driver had no PM ops and no .shutdown (E4). A channel left in manual
 mode by the regulator stayed in manual mode across a warm reboot until
 the regulator ran again, or for good if the module did not build for the
 new kernel (E9).
 .
 Adds a platform .shutdown hook. For every channel this module touched:
 - CPU (pwm1) and SSD (pwm2): EC automatic mode (0x21, 0x2e); the EC
   regulates them;
 - HDD (pwm3) and PCIe (pwm4): 255. PCIe: after its auto command (0x31)
   the EC keeps the last duty (befunde BEFUNDE.md). HDD, as a precaution:
   after 0x2b the EC regulates the group to a target RPM chosen from EC
   0x06 (ambient: < 34 C 1200 rpm, 34-99 C 1600 rpm), not from the disk
   temperatures (derived from EC firmware 0.14, befunde M5; the measured
   values fit). Returning them to "automatic" could undercut the
   regulator's fail-safe (n5-fangov: HDD 140) for the whole next boot if
   the module is not loaded again (E9 path), i.e. leave the fans lower
   than before (E3/E5 class, delta review finding 1).
 PCIe handed back with pwm4_enable=2 stays touched (0004) and is set to 255
 here again (audit-20261016 F-1). Unbind/unload (0004) also hands PCIe back
 at 255; HDD gets 0x2b there, CPU/SSD their auto command.
 A failed step is logged and leaves that channel as it is; there is no
 fallback to the auto command, which could lower the duty. The hook sets
 the dead flag under data->lock first: later hwmon/debugfs accesses return
 -ENODEV and the devres restore from 0004 does nothing afterwards. Every
 channel gets its own access budget from 0005 (<= 4 x 1 s in total).
 The same applies to poweroff (HDD/PCIe briefly at 255 before power-off).
 No suspend/resume ops: the host does not suspend (README, E4).
 .
 Consequence to verify (T6): after a warm reboot HDD and PCIe run at 255
 until n5-fangov sets its values; CPU/SSD are in EC automatic. Whether the
 EC or the BIOS keeps or resets these duties across the reboot is not
 measured.
 .
 Resolves E4 (driver side), E9 (no unregulated low duty across reboot).
 .
 Tested: build/static analysis as 0001. Not tested on hardware: warm
 reboot and poweroff with channels in manual mode, dmesg of the shutdown
 (journal of the previous boot), DCR/RPM directly after the reboot before
 n5-fangov starts (T6).
 .
 rc3 (audit-20261016 BACKLOG #27): header and code comment no longer say
 that the EC does not regulate HDD after 0x2b ("fixed 0x57"); that
 statement was corrected in befunde BEFUNDE.md on 2026-10-08/09 (M5).
 HDD 255 at shutdown is kept as a precaution. Comment text only; the
 code, the PCIe reasoning and the line count are unchanged.
